  "candidateComparison": "All 105 actual scenes match production on SQLite and real PostgreSQL, including ordinary owned Audio, AudioBook and Book targets with explicit or default owner parents and requested source deletion; pinned Audio OwnerId and malformed non-folder ParentId persistence-only closures; a stored non-Video PrimaryVersionId that does not create a video-version lifecycle; and mutable live Audio IsVirtualItem state that leaves the persisted source identity unchanged. DB-only and requested source deletion covers Series, Season, BoxSet, LiveTvProgram, MusicAlbum, Photo and PhotoAlbum; recursive Series, MusicAlbum and PhotoAlbum cleanup; six internal by-name item types; and physical MusicArtist DB-only, requested source and child cleanup. Source deletion covers mapped container directories, exact LiveTvProgram/Photo files, mixed Photo sidecars, managed BoxSet state, missing sources and source/external/SQL failure prefixes. Existing source-capable scenes retain the exact Episode Path versus other non-mixed Video containing directories, mixed-folder sidecars, Unicode prefixes and optional/enumeration failure prefixes. Candidate internal-path containment is deliberately stricter than native by requiring an instance path strictly below its exact type root; managed BoxSet state similarly requires a child below DataPath/collections. Candidate adapter controls verify readonly/root ID bindings, complete weak listings, optional permission/protocol failures, overlays, ID-only aliases, persisted/live source drift, and withheld Episode/Trailer directory discs. The two closure scenes remove descendant rows and warm cache entries without descendant file cleanup or Removed events; they do not establish a complete owned-extra or version-family lifecycle.",
